Happy Monday team!!

Big week ahead and honestly the pipeline is looking healthier than it has all year, so here's the Monday rundown. Nothing here needs anything from anyone, just keeping everyone in the loop!

MERIDIAN FOODS - pilot wrap-up is Wednesday. Carla's team at Salinas has been opening the exception report every morning shift, and their line lead told Ana it found the case packer issue nobody had suspected. Music to my ears! Carla mentioned Yuma (their second plant) again on Friday's call. Nothing formal yet, but the interest is real and I can feel it.

RIDGEWAY METALS - Ana's on touch #3 with Dale Whitcombe (Ops Director). No reply yet, but I got him for two minutes at the county manufacturers' breakfast last week and he told me he "doesn't do software", which in my experience is what people say six weeks before they buy software. Old-school shop, phone beats email there, Ana's calling Thursday.

CALDER TEXTILES (Reno) - NEW! Inbound from the website. Ruth Amsel, VP Ops, three plants, filled out the form at 11pm on a Saturday which tells you everything you need to know. Discovery call booked for Thursday, Ana's running it.

BLUEFIN SEAFOODS (Seattle) - also inbound (two in one week!!). Cold-chain processing, wants to see line telemetry plus exception alerts. Demo next week with Yuki. I'm running point on this one so Ana can focus on Calder and Ridgeway.

BRIGHTLINE - quarterly check-in Thursday, Yuki's got it. Usage is up 18% month over month. Green green green.

HALBERD - Yuki's data-mapping workshop with Renee's team is Friday. The plant contact list came through over the weekend, so we're set.

Numbers: 14 open opportunities, $1.1M weighted (up from $890k a month ago!), 4 pilots running. Q4 is going to be a push but if two of the pilots convert it's our best quarter yet, and I definately think two convert.

Also! I'm putting together a Q4 events list (a couple of regional manufacturing shows, the customer roundtable, one podcast). More on that when it's ready.

Have a great week everyone!!

